🍅 Tomato Plant Leaf Disease Detection

About the Project

Tomato Plant Leaf Disease Detection is an AI-based project that uses deep learning and computer vision to identify diseases in tomato plants by analyzing images of their leaves. The main goal is to develop an intelligent and user-friendly system that helps farmers, gardeners, and agricultural enthusiasts recognize potential plant diseases quickly and efficiently.

The project focuses on training an image classification model to recognize different tomato leaf conditions and predict the corresponding disease from an uploaded image.

🎯 Project Objectives

- Develop a deep learning model for tomato leaf disease classification.
- Detect and classify different tomato leaf diseases from images.
- Build an accessible system that can assist users in identifying plant health problems.
- Develop a mobile application for convenient, on-the-go disease detection.
- Expand the system to support additional plant species in future versions.

🚀 Planned Features

- Image-based tomato leaf disease detection.
- Deep learning-powered image classification.
- User-friendly interface for uploading and analyzing leaf images.
- Mobile application for disease detection using a smartphone camera.
- Future support for multiple plant species and diseases.
- Potential integration of disease information and prevention recommendations.

🛠️ Technologies

The project may use the following technologies:

- Python — Model development and data processing.
- PyTorch or TensorFlow — Deep learning and image classification.
- OpenCV — Image processing and computer vision.
- Flask or FastAPI — Backend API development.
- Mobile development technologies — For the future mobile application.

🗺️ Future Roadmap

1. Develop and evaluate the tomato leaf disease detection model.
2. Improve classification accuracy and test the model on unseen images.
3. Build a web-based interface or API for model predictions.
4. Develop a mobile application for easy access to disease detection.
5. Extend the model to identify diseases in other plants.
6. Explore disease prevention guidance and broader AI-powered agricultural solutions.

🌱 Vision

The long-term vision is to build an AI-powered plant disease detection platform that makes plant health monitoring more accessible, supports early disease identification, and contributes to smarter agricultural practices.

Project Status: Under Development

Contributions, suggestions, and feedback are welcome!
